"""Net part 4b: the transport's connections and their manager (net/net_transport.cpp lines 16-end) against the
original's (net/trans_diff.cpp, suite net.trans; run with HD2_TRANS_QUICK=1 on build_trans.bat, every file built with
-include sock_fakes.h, linked with -Wl,--image-base=0x20000000 -lws2_32).

245 mutants, 19 not building; 219 of the 226 building killed. The first run left 9: Receive's null for none (78 del:
the test had set it null itself), ReceiveAll's FlushDelayed between datagrams (363 del: the clock never moved within a
call; recvfrom moves it now). The 7 left:
- Unobservable: the destructors' DeleteCriticalSection (54, 271 del); a Leave without its Enter in ResendAll and
  FindByAddress (238, 322 del: today's Windows ignores leaving a section the thread does not own; one thread cannot
  tell).
- Equivalent: Receive's clearing of the packet's size before releasing it (87 del, num: nothing reads it before Clear
  sets it 0); Remove moving the last connection into its own place (381 cmp)."""
